# Line endings for files that are executed rather than read.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails inside a Linux container with
# "bad interpreter: no such file or directory" -- the \r becomes part of the
# interpreter path. Git stores LF in the index regardless, so a Linux checkout is
# normally fine, but that depends on every contributor's core.autocrlf rather
# than on anything in the repo. This states it instead.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
